 ],
 "description": "THE META-SHAPE GRAIN'S GROWTH LADDER. SHAPE_AUDIT.md finding #1: the agent's meta-shape vocabulary is a closed, hand-authored 11-entry table with no mint path anywhere in the tree \u2014 'the sd loop's fourth rung is not wired to the faculty named shape'. This seed wires the whole four-rung Occam ladder at that grain by pointing the UNCHANGED ShapeDecode / TransformDecode / DimInfer Terms at codebook_type='MetaShape' (load_parts is grain-agnostic), with the FIXED keyword scorer as the bootstrap rung below them and a new MetaShapeMint Term as rung 4. Emitted by tools/build_meta_shape_growth_seed.py.",
 "microtheory": {
  "name": "meta_shape_growth",
  "description": "the meta-shape codebook grows on residual"
 },
 "nodes": [],
 "edges": [],
 "productions": [
  {
   "provenance": "meta_shape_growth:observed_shape",
   "src": {
    "type": "Agent",
    "var": "ag"
   },
   "edge_type": "observed_shape",
   "tgt": {
    "type": "ShapeObservation",
    "var": "obs"
   }
  },
  {
